From 185d1ec07031099208dd82e0550aeabb07783654 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt port <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:15:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: ipq50xx: add support for Ruijie RG-MA3063

Ruijie RG-MA3063 is an AX3000 router, sold mainly as a China Mobile
customised unit. Hardware is close to the CMCC PZ-L8.

Specifications:
- SoC: Qualcomm IPQ5018 (board AP-MP02.1), dual-core A53
- RAM: 256 MiB DDR3
- Flash: 128 MiB SPI-NAND (Winbond, Macronix or FudanMicro FM25S01A)
- Ethernet: 4x 1GbE
  - socket 1 (next to the power jack): wan, IPQ5018 GE Phy (dp1)
  - sockets 2, 3 and the one printed "WAN": lan1-lan3, QCA8337 over
    SGMII (dp2)
- WiFi 2.4 GHz: IPQ5018 2x2 802.11ax
- WiFi 5 GHz: QCN6102 2x2 802.11ax
- LEDs: status green/blue/red
- Buttons: reset, WPS
- UART: 115200n8

MAC addresses come from the U-Boot env (0:appsblenv, ethaddr):
- LAN (dp2 conduit): ethaddr
- WAN (dp1): ethaddr + 1
- 2.4 GHz: ethaddr + 2
- 5 GHz: ethaddr + 3

Both radios use firmware memory mode 1 because of the 256 MiB RAM.

The FIT image carries a single configuration, config@mp02.1. Units whose
U-Boot looks for another configuration name will not boot this image.

Installation (UART):
1. Interrupt U-Boot, set ipaddr/serverip and serve the image via TFTP.
2. Test first: tftpboot 0x44000000 <initramfs-uImage.itb>; bootm 0x44000000
3. Flash both slots:
   tftpboot 0x44000000 <squashfs-factory.ubi>
   flash rootfs; flash rootfs_1; reset
Later upgrades use sysupgrade, which follows the QSDK A/B bootconfig.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0111edZhvhVsk8YZUqvNB7tj
